@startuml
' Publication as a state machine, before and after. The transition that did not
' exist is published -> published: publishing always created a fresh account, so a
' team could never be published a second time to the handle it already owned.
title Publishing a team — the transitions that existed, and the two that did not\n<size:11>a publication is the config record at rkey ""self""; the account and handle are separate, and survive it</size>

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam state {
  BorderThickness 1.5
  FontColor #263238
}

state "**BEFORE** — one way in, no way back" as Before #FFF8F8##[bold]C62828 {
  state "Never published" as B0 #line:455A64;back:ECEFF1
  B0 : no account, no config record
  B0 : ""GET …/published"" → 404

  state "Published" as B1 #line:2E7D32;back:E8F5E9
  B1 : account ""@handle"" exists on the PDS
  B1 : config record at rkey ""self"" names a **uri**
  B1 : an @mention triggers a run

  state "Answering, but gone" as B2 #line:C62828;back:FFEBEE
  B2 : removed from the wallet's team index
  B2 : config record still present
  B2 : replies from a dashboard it no longer appears in

  state "Refused" as B3 #line:C62828;back:FFEBEE
  B3 : ""400 InvalidRequest:""
  B3 : ""Handle already taken""

  state "Serving an older build" as B4 #line:EF6C00;back:FFF3E0
  B4 : a later deploy minted a new uri
  B4 : the config record still names the old one
  B4 : ""is_latest_deployment: false""

  [*] -[#455A64]-> B0
  B0 -[#2E7D32]-> B1 : publish\n<size:10>""create_account"" — the only path</size>
  B1 -[#EF6C00]-> B4 : re-deploy
  B4 -[#C62828]-> B3 : publish again\n<size:10>**the prescribed remedy**</size>\n<size:10>the account already exists</size>
  B1 -[#C62828]-> B3 : publish again
  B1 -[#C62828]-> B2 : delete the team\n<size:10>reaches the chain only</size>
}

state "**AFTER** — a toggle, and a deletion that reaches both stores" as After #F6FFF7##[bold]2E7D32 {
  state "Never published" as A0 #line:455A64;back:ECEFF1
  A0 : no account, no config record
  A0 : ""GET …/published"" → 404

  state "Published" as A1 #line:2E7D32;back:E8F5E9
  A1 : ""active: true""
  A1 : an @mention triggers a run

  state "Dormant" as A2 #line:1565C0;back:E3F2FD
  A2 : ""active: false""
  A2 : config record deleted
  A2 : **account, handle and DID kept**
  A2 : the handle still resolves

  state "Serving an older build" as A4 #line:EF6C00;back:FFF3E0
  A4 : ""is_latest_deployment: false""
  A4 : reported, and now fixable

  state "Gone" as A3 #line:455A64;back:ECEFF1
  A3 : unpublished **first**, then deleted
  A3 : nothing left answering

  [*] -[#455A64]-> A0
  A0 -[#2E7D32]-> A1 : publish\n<size:10>creates the account</size>
  A1 -[#1565C0]-> A2 : unpublish\n<size:10>""deleteRecord"" of the config record</size>
  A2 -[#2E7D32]-> A1 : publish again\n<size:10>**signs in** to the existing account,</size>\n<size:10>""put""s the singleton record,</size>\n<size:10>takes the first free ""Embers N"" password</size>
  A1 -[#EF6C00]-> A4 : re-deploy
  A4 -[#2E7D32]-> A1 : publish again\n<size:10>re-points the record at the current uri</size>
  A1 -[#455A64]-> A3 : ""removeTeam""\n<size:10>unpublish, **then** delete</size>
  A2 -[#455A64]-> A3 : delete
}

Before -[#455A64]right-> After : ""d938999"" + ""643066d""

note bottom of After #E3F2FD
  **Why Dormant keeps the account.** Deleting the atproto account would also stop the
  mentions, and it is the wrong operation: it frees the handle irreversibly, so anyone
  may take it. "Stop responding" should not mean "surrender your name". The credential
  on chain is not removed either, because it **cannot** be — the env contract keeps
  firesky tokens in a stack exposing only ""push"" and ""toList"". A publication is
  permanent history; what varies is whether the config record is present, and that is
  exactly what ""active"" reports.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#E8F5E9>| answering mentions, correctly |
  |<#E3F2FD>| deliberately silent, reversible |
  |<#FFF3E0>| answering, but not the current build |
  |<#FFEBEE>| wrong: a dead end, or a team that outlived itself |
  |<#ECEFF1>| nothing published |
endlegend
@enduml
